# XR Glasses Feature — pose, stabilization, geometry

Applies when touching the XR glasses support: pose provider interface, 3DoF
fusion, stabilization modes, geometry presets, head-tracked viewport, XR
settings UI, glasses detection.

**Docs (if stuck):** read `.cursor/rules/viture-glasses.mdc` and
`.cursor/rules/xreal-glasses.mdc` for the transports; behavior references:
https://github.com/pocket-xr/pocket-xr/blob/main/docs/GLASSES.md ·
https://github.com/wheaney/decky-xRGaming

## Settled design decisions (grill session, 2026-11-13)

1. **Three stabilization modes**: body-lock (stabilization off), smooth-follow
   (damped), world-lock (pinned; look around). Recenter action in all modes.
2. **Geometry presets, all 2D**: Single 1920×1080; Triple monitor 5760×1080
   (three discrete 1920×1080 zones, shell-enforced, visible gaps, farther
   apparent distance, world-locked); Ultrawide 3840×1080 (world-locked).
   Pan = head yaw/pitch clamped to canvas bounds.
3. **Triple-monitor escalation rule**: if zone enforcement in
   `CompositedWindowShell` proves too invasive during planning, DROP the
   triple preset and ship ultrawide — never silently degrade.
4. **Unified host-side pipeline both glasses**: pose provider interface →
   3DoF fusion in Kotlin → per-frame transform. Never rely on glasses'
   built-in stabilization for XR mode content.
5. **Injection point**: head-tracked crop/position on the glasses' mirror
   layer (`DisplayMirrorBackend.attachLayer` — `SurfaceControl.Transaction`
   per frame) over a logical desktop sized to the preset. Native Wayland
   compositor and Plasma shell stay untouched (except zone containment for
   triple monitor).
6. **Input**: phone-as-trackpad+keyboard role (existing) + physical
   mouse/keyboard passthrough (existing).
7. **UX**: per-glasses profile remembered, auto-applied on plug-in; XR card
   in display settings (mode, preset, recenter); XREAL one-time onboarding
   hint when Anchor detected.
8. **Performance bar**: solid 60 Hz; pose-driven crop every frame; light
   low-pass smoothing; 90/120 Hz opportunistic only.
9. **Generic fallback**: unrecognized glasses = plain external display
   behavior, zero stabilization, no crash.
10. **No proprietary SDK blobs** — community protocols only (GPL-3.0 FOSS).

## Package layout (T01+)

Pose types and the provider seam live in Kotlin package
`moe.n4tsu.dextop.xr`: `XrPoseProvider` / `AbstractXrPoseProvider` /
`XrPoseProviders` (in-memory registry) / `FakeXrPoseProvider` (tests only).
Production registers nothing until a device adapter task. Registry tests call
`XrPoseProviders.clearForTests()`.

## Detection + session (T02+)

Identity ids: `viture-pro` (VID `0x35CA` + PID `0x101D`, or a `viture` display
name), `viture` (other `0x35CA` PID), `xreal` (VID `0x3318`, or a link host
starting with `169.254.2.`, or an `xreal`/`nreal` display name). Family id is
`xreal` for every XREAL/Nreal model. Do not key the card on the USB product
string or on a single PID — EDID and strings vary (`Air 2 Pro` has no
`xreal` in the panel name). PID and NIC-vs-HID pick the transport later.

USB beats name. When both a Viture USB device and an XREAL signal (VID or
link) are present, any `xreal`/`nreal` display name wins the tie; otherwise
keep the Viture id.

Profiles: SharedPreferences name `dextop_xr`, keys `mode.<id>` /
`preset.<id>`. Modes `body-lock`|`smooth-follow`|`world-lock`; presets
`single`|`ultrawide`|`triple`. Auto-apply = load into the in-memory session on
identity change even if the settings card is closed.

USB permission for Viture HID uses action
`moe.n4tsu.dextop.xr.USB_PERMISSION` (separate from Linux USB). A
`USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED` device-filter meta-data entry is ignored unless the
activity also declares a matching intent-filter — that filter can foreground
`MainActivity` on plug-in. Recording that a permission dialog was shown is not
the same as granted; never re-ask on a poll loop — only on an explicit UI
action after clearing still-denied device ids.

Glasses session refresh on display hotplug must not depend on the overlay /
root view existing; hotplug can land with no overlay.

Flutter channel methods on `app.freedextop/display`: `xrGlassesState`,
`setXrGlassesProfile`, `xrGlassesRecenter`, `xrGlassesRequestUsbPermission`.

## Invariants

- Pose providers stream **3DoF orientation** (yaw/pitch/roll or quaternion);
  6DoF is out of scope.
- Fusion and smoothing are **host-side, in Kotlin** — never assume the
  glasses will stabilize for you.
- Glasses display is identified **before** XR features activate; unknown
  glasses degrade to generic external display.
- Mode switches (2D↔SBS, refresh) on the glasses cause HPD/EDID churn —
  Dextop does not toggle them (2D only).

## Symptom / cause / fix skeleton

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Content moves twice as fast as head / cut off at sides | Glasses in own world-lock mode while host also transforms (double transform) | One-series: Follow + Stabilizer off, detect via panel duty. Air has no Anchor mode, so this row does not apply to it |
| Screen drifts slowly over minutes | IMU yaw drift uncorrected | Recenter, plus a stationary gyro-bias estimate. Air mag is ignored, so do not add a magnetometer fusion to chase this row |
| Panning feels jittery | Raw pose fed to crop without smoothing | Low-pass pose before crop; tune damping; re-test at 60 Hz |
| Look-around shows black past canvas edge | Crop clamped but offset not | Clamp viewport offset to canvas bounds minus panel size |
| HID reader dies about 1s after open, or the next submit throws "currently queued" | `UsbDeviceConnection.requestWait(timeout)` throws and leaves the UsbRequest queued | Catch the timeout. Do not clear or requeue. Wait again on that request. |
| Interrupt OUT write succeeds and the IN endpoint stays empty | Interrupt IN read went through bulkTransfer | Read interrupt IN with UsbRequest. bulkTransfer is fine for interrupt OUT. |
| Next plug cannot reclaim the HID interface | Connection closed while a request wait was still in flight | Cancel the request, join the reader, then release and close. |
| USB Allow dialog never appears while only the glasses panel is lit | The system permission UI opened on the built-in panel, and that panel is off | Wake the phone. The dialog is already there. Do not reinstall to ask again. |
| HID interface flaps every couple of seconds after a failed open | Each display snapshot starts a new claim while the same device is still attached | Latch that device until it detaches. Clear the latch on unplug. |

